    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2FSQZoNBfQ8ZYkxVh7C8Wx5)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Base: `main` (includes #487 and #489). Depends on nothing open.\n- The branch is numbered `490-…` and needs no rename.\n- After merging: run the dry run on one `.bib` file and read it before applying (see \"Not applied yet\").\n\n## Summary\n\n- **Request:** a function in the BibTeX lint that takes the Zotero paths in `file` fields, matches each PDF to the copy already in `literature/inbox/zotero-backup`, moves it to the top of `literature/`, rewrites the field, and moves the record in DEVONthink too. Modelled on the earlier `bdsk` fix.\n- **New module `sp-bibtex-zotero`** (own doc `docs/tangles/academic/sp-bibtex-zotero.org`, bullet lists; the module is separate because `sp-bibprocess.el` is already about 2,600 lines). Required from `sp-academic`.\n- **Keys** (`C-; L b z`, same verbs as every lint group): `l` dry run, `a` apply (`C-u` also the weak matches), `r` restore a run.\n- **What the real data looks like** (read-only look at `~/Documents/bibliography` and `~/Documents/literature`):\n  - The \"6-digit encoding\" is an **8-character Zotero key** (`A-Z0-9`, for example `Z6HVLKNU`). All 3,926 Zotero paths in the 80 `.bib` files use it (`sp-bibtex-zotero-key-regexp` if that ever changes).\n  - 3,879 of those paths have a folder in `zotero-backup`; the folder normally holds the PDF and Zotero cache files (`.zotero-ft-cache` and so on).\n  - Path forms handled: bare `/Users/…/Zotero/storage/KEY/name.pdf`, Zotero's `label:path:mime`, several parts joined with `;`, BibTeX escapes (`\\;`), wrapped lines, another user's home (`/Users/clb3/…`).\n- **Matching** (names only, no guessing): `exact`, `normalised` (case, spacing, accents, TeX accents like `{\\\"i}`, curly quotes and dashes), then two **weak** levels shown for review only (`by-dir`: the only file of that type in the folder; `by-name`: no folder, but exactly one file of that name in the whole backup). Otherwise reported as `no-dir`, `no-file` (Zotero caches only), `ambiguous`, `collision` or `unsafe-name`.\n- **Dry-run numbers from a Python mirror of these rules on the real files** (nothing was written; the Elisp itself has not run on the real library):\n  - 1,824 sure matches, which are 1,426 distinct PDFs (several entries share one file);\n  - 11 weak matches for review; 34 paths with no folder and no file of that name; 50 whose folder has no PDF;\n  - 19 destination names clash between different backup folders (6 identical files, 13 different), so the 13 would be reported as `collision` and not moved; no clash with a file already at the top of `literature/`;\n  - 1,408 `.html` snapshots and 75 `.epub` and other files are left alone (`sp-bibtex-zotero-extensions`, default `(\"pdf\")`).\n- **Safety**:\n  - dry run changes nothing; the plan is an Org table report built with `sp-batch-report-table-section` (rows link to the entry; `d` drops a row from the plan, `u` brings it back, `g` refreshes, `A` or `C-c C-c` applies);\n  - only adds or modifies: no file or record is deleted; a file is never moved over another; a clash is reported, or, for an identical file already at the top, only the field is rewritten (the backup copy stays);\n  - apply copies the `.bib` file first (same backup folder as the other lint fixes) and writes a manifest (`zotero-manifest.eld`) **before** moving, so a cut-short run can still be restored; if the move fails half way, the files that did move are still rewritten and the error is shown;\n  - `restore` moves the files back and puts the earlier `.bib` text back; it refuses if the `.bib` file changed after the run, and keeps the current text as `before-restore.bib`;\n  - **DEVONthink**: moves go through `tools/devonthink-move.py` (PR #410) with `--plain-rename`, so records keep UUID, tags and highlights. The dry run asks the tool for its own dry run (records to move, files not in DEVONthink, blocked). Apply and restore **refuse before touching anything** when `sp-bibtex-files-devonthink-tool` is unset or DEVONthink is not running (checked with `pgrep`, so DEVONthink is never launched by accident); `sp-bibtex-zotero-require-devonthink` turns that off.\n- No `CHANGELOG.org` edit (nightly tidy), `when-let*`/`if-let*` only, no `.el` edited by hand (tangled from the docs; `tools/tangle-all.el` gives no drift for the three docs touched).\n\n## Not applied yet\n\n- **The real library was not touched.** Please read the dry-run output on your Mac first and approve it before anyone runs `a`.\n- Not run on the Mac: the Elisp against your real `.bib` files, and the AppleScript of `devonthink-move.py` on this plan (it is the existing, merged tool; this PR only calls it). The container has no DEVONthink.\n- Open on the Mac: DEVONthink needs a group for the top-level `literature` folder (the tool stops with `no group for …` otherwise).\n\n## Tested\n\n- New `tests/sp-bibtex-zotero-test.el`, Emacs 29.3 batch: 22 pass. Covers parsing (labels, mime, escapes, wrapped lines, other users), name matching, every match level, plan classes, clashes, an existing file at the top, unsafe names, a dry run that changes nothing, drop, aligned Org tables, apply (moves, rewrites, snapshots and weak/unmatched paths untouched), weak apply, never overwriting, identical-file link, refusing without DEVONthink, partial failure, idempotence (including a move seen only in the manifest), and restore (round trip, refusal after an edit).\n- `tests/sp-keys-test.el`: 5 pass (one new for `C-; L b z`). `sp-batch-report-test`: 22 pass.\n- Not run: the GUI, which-key labels, `sp-bibprocess-lint-test` (it fails to load in the container on `main` as well: `void-variable sp-cache-dir`).\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [ ] Pull this branch, restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`) (untested by Claude)\n- [ ] `C-; L b z` then `C-h`: which-key shows `l`, `a`, `r`; the label `zotero paths` is under `C-; L b` (untested by Claude)\n- [ ] Open `humanities.bib` and press `C-; L b z l`: the `*Zotero paths*` report opens, nothing is written (`git -C ~/Documents/bibliography status` is clean)\n- [ ] The summary says how many files would move; the DEVONthink line gives records to move, files not in DEVONthink and blocked\n- [ ] Spot-check 5 rows of \"To move\" against Finder: the Zotero path, the file in `zotero-backup/KEY/`, the new name\n- [ ] Check \"Review\", \"Not matched\" and the collisions: nothing there is applied by `A`\n- [ ] `RET` on a row visits the entry in the `.bib`; `d` on a row drops it, `u` brings it back, `g` makes the plan again\n- [ ] Quit DEVONthink, press `A` or `C-; L b z a`: it refuses with \"DEVONthink is not running\" and nothing changes\n- [ ] Safe trial: copy one `.bib` and 3 PDFs (with their `KEY` folders) to a scratch library, set `sp-literature-dir` to it, run `a` with DEVONthink open\n- [ ] After the trial: the PDFs are at the top of the scratch library, the fields say `name.pdf`, the backup folder has no PDFs left in those `KEY` folders, the `.bib` copy and `zotero-manifest.eld` are in `sp-bibtex-lint-backup-directory`\n- [ ] In DEVONthink the moved records keep their tags and highlights (same UUID, now in the `literature` group)\n- [ ] `C-; L b z r` puts the files and the `.bib` back; run it twice: the second time says there is nothing to restore\n- [ ] Edge: edit the `.bib` after an apply, then `r`: it refuses and tells you where the copy is\n- [ ] Edge: `C-u C-; L b z a` also applies the weak matches (check one in the dry run first)\n- [ ] Only after reading the real dry run: apply on the real library, one `.bib` file at a time\n\n<details><summary>Revert after testing</summary>\n\n- Restore a run: `C-; L b z r` (moves back through DEVONthink, puts the earlier `.bib` back).\n- By hand: the `.bib` copy and `zotero-manifest.eld` are in `sp-bibtex-lint-backup-directory/<stamp>/`; the manifest lists every move as `(FROM . TO)`.\n- Discard local edits: `git -C ~/dotfiles status`, then `git -C ~/dotfiles restore .`.\n- Return to main: `git -C ~/dotfiles switch main` and `git -C ~/dotfiles pull`; optionally `git -C ~/dotfiles branch -D 490-zotero-paths-to-literature`.\n- Restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`).\n\n</details>\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiCGfFMGGDntzUxNQTU)_",
